Student Council Goals
The Student Council exists to represent the interests and feelings of its constituents (class members, club officers, faculty and staff members) in regard to all matters related to school improvement including:
1. A school program that is relevant to student needs, and that gives each member an equal opportunity for development of his/her potential, both academically and socially;
2. A program of activities that is balanced and that meets the needs and interests of the student body as a whole;
3. An atmosphere in which the school and its program are promoted in such a manner as to make the student aware of school programs and policies and to create interest in them;
